# WARP-8's flow on a kit. HOME: a row a drum; ALGORITHM picks the drum, a black key mutes one, knob 4 and PRESETS the
# kit, knob 2 every drum's length, knob 1 the tempo. SEQ: PRESETS the pattern; a lane held, knob 4 its own length.
# HOME held, ALGORITHM is the track
wait 300
listen
expect trk 1
tap HOME
wait 40
expect page Arrange
turn ALGO 2
wait 40
said DRUM
tapkey b3
wait 40
expect kmute 8
tapkey b3
wait 40
expect kmute 0
# the kit: knob 4, then PRESETS (Loom, Nylon, Elastane); the first drum's model follows
turn K4 1
wait 60
said KIT
expect par1.d1.model 11
turn PRESET 1
wait 60
expect par1.d1.model 20
turn PRESET -1
turn PRESET -1
wait 60
expect par1.d1.model 0
turn K1 1
wait 40
expect tempo 121
shot kithome.png
# (four kits tried so far: four hits heard.) A kick on step 1 of 16: one hit a bar; its own length four: four a bar; HOME's length for every drum: one again
tap SEQ
wait 40
tapkey b0
tapkey w0
expect drumhits 5
tap PLAY
wait 1700
tap PLAY
expect drumhits 6
key b0 down
wait 100
turn K4 -12
wait 60
key b0 up
wait 40
shot kitflow_ownlen.png
expect drumhits 7
tap PLAY
wait 1700
tap PLAY
expect drumhits 11
tap HOME
wait 40
turn K2 -1
turn K2 1
wait 40
tap PLAY
wait 1700
tap PLAY
expect drumhits 12
# SEQ: PRESETS is the pattern
tap SEQ
wait 40
turn PRESET 1
wait 40
# HOME held: the track
press HOME
turn ALGO 1
release HOME
wait 40
expect trk 2
